# Overview

Insert overview text here. The agent will only see this should they choose to apply the rule.
Applies to all work. No exceptions.

1. System Separation
	•	FXG = Mac-only, long-term design, architecture + dashboard perfection.
	•	GCLOUD = VM-only, trade-ready, operational robustness.
	•	Never mix code/config unless an explicit porting task is declared.

2. Brutal Truth Standard
	•	No guessing.
	•	No mock or placeholder data.
	•	Any claim MUST have proof: file path, command output, logs, or screenshots.
	•	If proof is missing → FAIL, not “partial”.

3. Safety First (Non-Negotiable)
	•	Trading is OFF by default.
	•	Required gates:
TRADING_ENABLED, DRY_RUN, PAPER/PRACTICE, daily limits.
	•	If a kill switch is missing → BLOCKED.

4. No Placeholder Rule
	•	No “coming soon”, no fake users, no static demo text.
	•	Missing backend data must render as explicit empty state.
	•	Required feature + missing backend = FAIL.

5. Work Method (Always)
	1.	Inventory
	2.	Plan
	3.	Patch
	4.	Verify
	5.	Lock & document
No step may be skipped.

6. Configuration Canon
	•	One central config location only.
	•	No secrets hardcoded.
	•	APIs must be replaceable without code edits.
	•	If a key appears in code → remove it.

7. Clean-Room Enforcement (GCLOUD)
	•	All work happens in ~/gcloud_clean_room.
	•	Never patch legacy/messy folders.
	•	VM deploys start in DRY_RUN only.

8. Verification Requirement

Every milestone must end with:
	•	PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED
	•	Evidence list (commands, logs, screenshots)
	•	Clear next action owner (YOU or CURSOR)

9. Dashboard Truth
	•	UI reflects only what backend emits.
	•	No inferred or derived UI values unless explicitly produced.
	•	Browser verification is mandatory.

10. Default Model Choice (Your Sonnet List)
	•	Sonnet 4.5 → complex reasoning, safety gates, multi-step refactors (default)
	•	Sonnet 4 → fast mechanical edits, grep/replace tasks